Disease risk model implemented as a documented threshold/scoring MVP, not
a trained classifier or image CNN, per the roadmap's locked scope
decision 5. decisions/0009-disease-risk-model.md documents the weighted
scoring system (humidity 0.40, rainfall 0.25, temperature 0.15, NDVI
trend 0.20 over FeatureVector fields), the risk-level thresholds, the
confidence-as-evidence-completeness formula, and the CNN upgrade path.

src/agro_mirai/models/disease_risk_scoring.py holds the pure
score_disease_risk(FeatureVector) -> DiseaseRiskScore function.
src/agro_mirai/models/disease_risk_model.py wraps it as
DiseaseRiskModel.predict(FeatureVector) -> DiseaseRiskAlert, matching
Modules 06/07's calling convention exactly (no trained artifact to load,
unlike 06/07 — this module has no models/*.joblib).

16 tests in tests/models/: 9 unit tests on the scoring function in
isolation (known-input -> known-risk-level, schema-independent), 5
wrapper tests (schema-valid output via check_specs.py's validation
logic), 2 integration tests (farm-001/farm-002 fixture -> FeatureBuilder
-> DiseaseRiskModel -> schema-valid DiseaseRiskAlert, end to end). All
pass. Full suite: 119 passed, 0 failed, 25 skipped (voice, needs .venv).

Acceptance checklist:
- [x] Fixture outputs are agronomically plausible: farm-001 (69% 14d
      mean humidity, 6.6mm 7d rainfall, temp near the 25C fungal
      optimum) scores 0.365 -> moderate; farm-002 (63% humidity, 0mm
      rain, no NDVI) scores 0.254 -> low, with lower confidence (0.7 vs
      1.0) correctly reflecting the missing NDVI signal.
- [x] Not input-invariant: test_score_is_not_constant_across_inputs
      pins a synthetic low-risk input (40% humidity, no rain, 10C) at
      "low"/<0.30 and a synthetic high-risk input (90% humidity, 40mm
      rain, 25C, -0.08 NDVI trend) at "severe"/>=0.70 — different
      levels, not just different scores.
- [x] CNN upgrade path is additive: DiseaseRiskAlert's schema fields
      (disease, risk_level, confidence, window_*, recommended_action)
      don't need to change shape for a future image-based model — see
      ADR 0009's "CNN upgrade path" section, field-by-field.

